sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch02-12> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Historical ornamental art contains many repetitive patterns and some nested ones, but the more complicated patterns produced by simple cellular automata such as rule 30 never appear to have been used.";
    dc:type "prediction";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Complex cellular-automaton-like patterns are absent from historical ornament";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 2, “The Crucial Experiment”; section “Why These Discoveries Were Not Made Before” (from p. 42), p. 43. Scope: historical ornamental art across cultures"
}
